              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em idempotent monad
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            that “squares to itself” in the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            sense. Idempotent monads hence serve as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            operators, in that they encode
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
            and the reflection/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            onto these.
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            idempotent monads interpret (co-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operators"}> modal operators
            ; see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          #IdempotentMonad.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong idempotent monad
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\mu,\eta)
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              such that one (hence all) of the following equivalent statements are true:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi T
                        %mi T
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\colon T T \to T
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  All components of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi T
                        %mi T
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \,\colon\, T T \to T
                  are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi η
                        %mo ,
                        %mi η
                        %mi T
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi T
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\eta, \eta T \,\colon\, T \to T T
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
                  (that is,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo ,
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \eta)
                  is a
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+endofunctor"} well-pointed endofunctor
              %li
                %p
                  For every
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebra
                  (aka:
                  = succeed "-module)" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo ,
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M,u)
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi T
                        %mi M
                        %mo →
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon T M \to M
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  (i.e. every algebra is a
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi T
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^T \to \mathcal{C}
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^T
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
                  of
                  = succeed "-algebras)" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %li
                %p
                  There exists a pair of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \dashv U
                  such that the induced monad
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi U
                        %mi F
                        %mo ,
                        %mi μ
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi U
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                        %mo ,
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T \colon U F, \mu \coloneqq U \epsilon F, \eta)
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo ,
                        %mi μ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\mu, \eta)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
                %p#SixPrime 6’.
                %p
                  There is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi T
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon C^T \hookrightarrow C
                  and a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ,
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mo ∼
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo ,
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi f
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↦
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi η
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi f
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        Hom_{\mathcal{C}}\big(
                        T(c)
                        ,\,
                        U(a)
                        \\big)
                        \&amp;
                        \\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}
                        \&amp;
                        Hom_{\mathcal{C}}\big(
                        c
                        ,\,
                        U(a)
                        \\big)
                        \\\
                        \\big(
                        T(c) \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} U(a)
                        \\big)
                        \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                        \\big(
                        c
                        \\overset{\eta}{\longrightarrow}
                        T(c)
                        \\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}
                        U(a)
                        \\big)
                        }
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    (This is the form in which
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operators"} modal operators
                    tend to be axiomatized in
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
                    = succeed ".)" do
                      %a{:href => "modal+homotopy+type+theory#HoTTBook"} UP13, Def. 7.7.1
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi T
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi T
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T T \Rightarrow T T
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Borceux"}> Borceux, prop. 4.2.3
            ). For (7) see Lemma 3.4 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RosebrughWood95"} RW95
          #EquivalentConditions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The conditons in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IdempotentMonad"}
              are indeed equivalent.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_in_more_than_one_way Proof (in more than one way).
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\Rightarrow 2
                %p This is trivial.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\Rightarrow 3
                %p
                  Compositions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi T
                        %mi η
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\circ T\eta
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi η
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\circ\eta T
                  are always the identity (unit axioms for the monad), and in particular agree; if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
