          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Let us be in a
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,T,\eta,\mu)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is of course an idempotent morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T:C\to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              as part of the structure such that an idempotent 1-cell has a 2-isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo :
                    %mi TT
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu:TT\to T
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mi T
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu T=T\mu
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{*,e\}
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^2=e
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              Recall that a
              %em splitting of an idempotent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\mu)
              consists of a pair of 1-cells
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I:D\to C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:C\to D
              and a pair of 2-isomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:R I\to id_D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:T\to I R
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu=b^{-1}(I\circ s\circ R)(b\circ b)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
              denotes horizontal composition of 2-cells. Equivalently an splitting of an idempotent is a limit or a colimit of the defining pseudofunctor. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              has equalizers or coequalizers, then all its idempotents split.
            %p
              Now if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (I,R,a,b)
              is a splitting of an idempotent monad, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\dashv I
              are adjoint. And in this case the splitting of an idempotent is equivalently an Eilenberg-Moore object for the monad
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mi η
                      %mo ,
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,T,\eta,\mu)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is called an
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  adjoint retract of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"}> Johnstone, B 1.1.9, p.248-249
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p Equivalences (resp. cores) in an allegory are precisely those symmetric idempotents which are idempotent monads (resp. comonads). In an allegory the following statements are equivalent: all symmetric idempotents split, idempotent monads split, idempotent comonads split. A similar statement holds at least for some 2-categories.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Given an algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo :
                    %mi TX
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, u:TX\to X)
              , by (1) and (4) the action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              yields an isomorphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^T
              between the free algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi TX
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (TX, \mu_X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,u)
              i.e. for an idempotent monad the Eilenberg-Moore and the Kleisli categories coincide.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#AlgebrasForAnIdempotentMonad Algebras for an idempotent monad and Localization
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \eta, \mu)
              be an idempotent monad on a category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  carries an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+a+monad"} algebra structure
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi e
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta e\colon e \to T e
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+monomorphism"} split monomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta e
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              (It follows from 3. that there is at most one algebra structure on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mi e
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mi e
                      %mo →
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi = (\eta e)^{-1}\colon T e \to e
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The implication 1.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              2. is immediate. Next, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi e
                    %mo →
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi\colon T e \to e
              is any retraction of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta e
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi η
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \circ \eta e = 1_e
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi η
                            %mi e
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi ξ
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mi ξ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mi T
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext naturality of
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi η
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mi ξ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mi η
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext see definitions above
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ξ
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi η
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext functoriality
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mi T
                                %mi e
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\eta e \circ \xi &amp; = &amp; (T \xi)(\eta T e) &amp; &amp; \text{naturality of}\, \eta \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; (T \xi)(T \eta e) &amp; &amp; \text{see definitions above} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; T(\xi \circ \eta e) &amp; &amp; \text{functoriality} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; 1_{T e} &amp; &amp;
                    }
            %p
              so 2. implies 3. Finally, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta e
              is an isomorphism, put
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mi e
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi = (\eta e)^{-1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi η
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \circ \eta e = 1_e
              (unit condition), and the associativity condition for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi μ
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \circ \mu e = \xi \circ T \xi,
            %p
              follows by inverting the naturality equation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mi T
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi η
                      %mi e
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %mi η
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi η
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta T e \circ \eta e = T \eta e \circ \eta e
          #ReflectiveSubcategoryOfIdempotentMonad.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              This means that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              (a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"}> localization
              ” of the ambient category) whose embedding-reflection
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              gives the idempotent monad.
          %p
            See also (
            %a{:href => "#Borceux"}> Borceux, volume 2, corollary 4.2.4
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              Hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dually
              the co-algebras over an idempotent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              form a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
              one thinks of a (idempotent) (co-)monad as a (co-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operator"} modal operator
              and of its algebras as (co-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+types"}> modal types
              \. In this terminology the above says that categories of (co-)modal types are precisely the (co-)reflective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizations"} localizations
              of the ambient type system.
          %h3#AssociatedIdemopotentMonad The associated idempotent monad of a monad
          %p
            We discuss here how under suitable conditions, for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            there is a “completion” to an idempotent monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde T
            in that the completion construction is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the inclusion of idempotent monads into the category of all monads on a given category, exhibiting the subcategory of idempotent monads as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
